{"kind":"report","text":"Approved exact head 44997a7524ed073da52c65c18cad26b997a22820, artifact 7e5f1387. The observation-relative invariant is now correct in both the crash table and test 17: the incorporation reference transaction never writes target_ref; success preserves target_pre_head; abort preserves the value present when the transaction began, including a racer-written value. This matches test 9 and removes the last contradiction. Everything accepted in the prior reviews is unchanged.\n\nArchitecture: layer 7 owns Git reachability, detector composition, the off-target receipt object, and the atomic update-ref --stdin transaction that verifies target_ref while creating receipt_ref. Layer 5 stays repository-independent and closes only the approval-named artifact through the signed prior receipt, without path succession. R2 and R3 correctly require same-head updates to architecture.md and merge.md where their contracts change.\n\nSecurity: the protocol is fail-closed at the relevant boundaries. Durable preflight checks batch shape and byte ceilings; the off-target object is unreferenced before commitment; one atomic Git transaction prevents both stale target_pre_head sealing and double spend; crashes before it leave no receipt ref, crashes after it are recoverable from complete trailers; retry validates exact approval, candidate, authorization pair, target pre-head, incorporation mode, parents, and empty succession fields; the durable append evaluates intervening workroom traffic against current state. The merge lock is not overclaimed as excluding external Git writers. No secret, signature, authority, bounds, or malformed-input defect remains. This design explicitly adopts nothing and claims no follow-on authority, so approval does not infer an authority-bearing adoption chain.\n\nSimplification: one off-target object, one atomic two-ref Git transaction, one receipt field, and one narrow fold clause reuse existing receipt and recovery machinery. There is no second closure system, reservation state, new lock, automatic acceptance, or path-wide retirement. No further simplification is available without weakening crash recovery or exact target verification.\n\nIndependent gates: branch and origin both equal 44997a7524ed073da52c65c18cad26b997a22820; merge-base is exact current main 860ee61a07aa753dcbc2d50e74da2b7b6547625b; exactly one commit and sole changed path notes/2026-08-31-merged-head-commitment-reconciliation.md; tree clean; git diff --check passes; make docs passes. Code citations to main.go:775, 780-786, 806-809, 822-824, 963-966, 698-712, 1576-1626 and mergeplan.go:954-955 were re-derived and remain correct.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:7e5f1387d7810714ee458ac5afe594c5a5a2cf06","head":"44997a7524ed073da52c65c18cad26b997a22820","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:a3dbe1606db38bf51c8a3eec47db8fe4740f1a00\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:a3dbe1606db38bf51c8a3eec47db8fe4740f1a00","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}